<title>USA: Cylink names Sarrat as president.</title>
<headline>Cylink names Sarrat as president.</headline>
<dateline>SUNNYVALE, Calif. 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cylink Corp said it named Fernand Sarrat as president and chief executive officer.</p>
<p>Sarrat, 45, succeeds Lewis Morris, 64, who retired in June 1996.</p>
<p>Sarrat was part of the senior management team on International Business Machines Corp's worldwide network services strategy. He started at IBM in sales and became director of marketing in Manhattan and general manager of marketing and services in the Midwest, where he was recognized for the rapid turnaround of an eight state, $2 billion, 3,000 person sales organization, Cylink said.</p>
</text>
